      "writtenOn": "2026-10-16T15:32:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WDYT about keeping `getLabel()` return the base label w/o the flags and adding a getter for the flags? My concern here is that we are returning a newly constructed `std::string` each time instead of a `const\u0026`.\n\nEventually I believe the only callers of `getLabel()` besides when updating the labels in `ResourceCache` or on the backend synchronization are going to be wrapping textures and pipelines.  We changed to returning a const std::string\u0026 for the pipeline labels so that tracing would have lower CPU time.\n\nAlternatively, we can switch `fLabel` to hold the full label including flags, which we build once in `setLabelInfo()`. When building the full label, we can remember the length of the base label (or infer the length of the appended flag strings from the flag mask later on) to be able to extract a string_view from the full label that is the base label.\n\nThat\u0027s my preference over a simpler implementation that just holds two std::strings (base and full, since they\u0027d overlap so much in content).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 304,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 309,
        "endChar": 75
      },
      "revId": "9f9a8d993f913b99eda1522c962a7c2218cbf24d",
